# CQ 19: What is a protocol data unit of a case made of?
#
# Clause 5.6.1 splits the unit into protocol control information and user data.
# The composition is what makes the layered architecture work: each layer adds
# its own control information and treats what it received as user data.
#
# Restricted to the units a case states something about. The catalogue supplies
# the named kinds of unit per layer, frame, packet, segment and the rest, and
# those describe what a unit at a layer is called rather than what a given
# communication carried. Anchoring on the transmission is what keeps the answer
# about the case.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?pdu ?controlInformation ?userData ?layerNumber
WHERE {
  ?communication iso7498:transmits ?pdu .
  ?pdu a iso7498:ProtocolDataUnit .
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:hasControlInformation ?controlInformation }
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:hasUserData ?userData }
  OPTIONAL { ?pdu iso7498:atLayer/iso7498:layerNumber ?layerNumber }
} ORDER BY ?pdu
